ial mansion constructed largely of wood, set in a pleasant, manicured garden. The lower floor has a collection of old tools, and an A/C room that has changing displays such as art exhibitions. The more…"],["Basilica of Santo Niño","sight",10.29402,123.90147,"Osmeña Boulevard","","","","","r","A large and venerable church that traces its history to the founding of the convent of the Santo Niño de Cebu in 1565. It contains a statue of the Santo Niño (Holy Child) that is regarded as the oldest religious relic in the…"],["Magellan's Cross","sight",10.29359,123.90195,"Plaza Sugbo, off Magallanes St","","","","","r","An octagonal building decorated with murals containing a large wooden cross that commemorates the Portuguese conquistador Ferdinand Magellan who planted a wooden cross upon converting the original inhabitants to Christianity. A plaque…"],["Cebu Metropolitan Cathedral","sight",10.29581,123.90287,"","","","","","r","A church built in 1565 by the first Spanish missionaries in Cebu, seat of an Archbishop who has subordinate Bishops in many cities of the Visayas. It was mostly destroyed during World War II and had been rebuilt a bit differently.…"],["Jose R. Gullas Halad Museum","sight",10.29697,123.90212,"","","","","","r","A museum that pays homage to the musical heritage of Cebu. This museum is operated under the Tipiganan sa mga Handumanan sa Kanta ug Kinaiyang Sugbuanon (Treasury of Memories) Foundation. In the old building of The Freeman Newspaper."],["Yap-Sandiego Ancestral House","sight",10.29929,123.90399,"Mabini St","","","","","r","Another historic house, this one from the 17th century, with hand-carved furniture and a garden. It does indeed look old/cryptic."],["Jesuit House Museum","sight",10.29861,123.90409,"26 Zulueta St","","","","","r","Yet another heritage house museum, this one the residence of a Jesuit from around 1730. Inside looks like a Spanish galleon."],["Sugbu Chinese Heritage Museum","sight",10.29244,123.902,"M.C. Briones St & Burgos St","","","","","r","Small exhibit hall on Chinese heritage in Cebu. This building (the Gotiaoco Building), also has a mural of the Magellan's Cross shrine and other Cebu highlights on its backside."],["Heritage of Cebu","sight",10.29885,123.90362,"Sikatuna St,","","","","","r","A massive and particularly detailed monument showcasing the heritage of Cebu from the old Spanish to the American colonial era."]]}